 0,0,0,0),nrow=R, ncol=J, byrow=TRUE)

I am wondering if it is ok to use a ZIP model when you do not have a lot of zeros in your data?  When I ran the global  P model  my c.hat showed that my data is highly overdispersed (C.hat >10), so I am reluctant to convert to QAIC and rank these models.  I tried the NB models but every time I increase my K, my population would increase and never seemed to stabilize.    When I ran ZIP models, I got the lowest AIC values and my data was not over dispersed.   Does anyone see a reason why I should not use the ZIP models?  I have pasted the top five results for the ZIP and P models below.

