hi Kyle,
 yes it would be ok to use the ZIP model in this case, although it should estimate a small fraction of zeros obviously.
 The bigger problem is that the within-site counts are distinctly not binomial, and when you try to soak up that variation by modeling variation in N then you wind up with this severe numerical instability problem that you noted.
 It would be better to pursue other observation models besides the binomial but we can't do that in unmarked (not because its not easy to do but, rather, because we probably won't get around to writing code for it anytime soon!).
regards
andy

